Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) to the creator
and/or subsequent owner(s) (each and all, an "owner") of an original work
of authorship and/or a database (each, a "Work").

Certain owners wish to permanently relinquish those rights to a Work for
the purpose of contributing to a commons of creative, cultural and
scientific works ("Commons") that the public can reliably and without fear
of later claims of infringement build upon, modify, incorporate in other
works, reuse and redistribute as freely as possible in any form whatsoever
and for any purposes, including without limitation commercial purposes.
These owners may contribute to the Commons to promote the ideal of a free
commons and the further production of creative, cultural and scientific
works, or without having a distinct purpose or motivation.

In furtherance of these purposes and desires, then, and in order to provide
a copyright notice and/or license that can be applied to world-wide public
domain dedications and successfully accommodate as many legal systems as
possible, the person associating CC0 with a Work (the "Affirmer"), to the
extent that he or she is the owner of Copyright and Related Rights in the
Work, voluntarily elects to apply CC0 to the Work and publicly distribute
the Work under its terms, with respect to those rights and all related
claims and causes of action under health, safety or environmental laws.

For the full legal text, please visit:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
